    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Following the May 3 medical entrance exam, an informant provided evidence to the National Testing Agency, a government agency, revealing a verified match between the chemistry paper and leaked PDFs. This evidence submission protocol prompted a referral to an investigative agency, leading to the arrest of detained suspects. The event outcome was the exam's cancellation and the scheduling of a corrective re-test for June 21, aimed at process restoration.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The initial test administration on May 3 was followed by a tip reception that substantiated a breach in the examination's integrity. An escalation to a verification authority resulted in a law enforcement outcome, with alleged conspirators now facing legal scrutiny. This sequence underscores the importance of a fact-verification body in safeguarding academic standards.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A disclosure from an evidence-bearer prompted the exam authority to initiate a procedural handoff to the state inquiry apparatus. The resulting arrests of accused individuals mark a consequence of the investigation. The planned re-examination stands as an integrity safeguard, seeking to restore a timeline disrupted by the breach.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
